{% comment %}
Shared display primitives for the four TRMNL viewports.

These templates only format already-normalized display values. They deliberately
refuse to supply defaults for absent metrics: a missing value stays invisible
rather than turning into a plausible-looking zero.
{% endcomment %}

{% template progress_rail %}
  {% if progress %}
    <div class="progress progress-bar {{ size | escape }}">
      <div class="track">
        <div class="fill" style="width: {{ progress | escape }}%"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% template alert_marker %}
  {% if alert %}
    <div class="item item--emphasis-2">
      <div class="content">
        <span class="value value--xsmall">! ALERT</span>
        {% if show_detail %}
          <span class="description">{{ alert | escape }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The full view's bottom strip. The framework reserves space for a `.title_bar`
  there, so it is always rendered: omitting it when there is nothing to report
  leaves the content floating in a screen taller than it expects.

  The timestamp is the bridge's, in UTC, and labelled as such. The obvious
  alternative is the device's own clock, but that shows when the screen was
  drawn rather than when the data was read, which is precisely the distinction
  a freshness stamp exists to make.
{% endcomment %}
{% template plugin_footer %}
  <div class="title_bar">
    <span class="title">
      Bambu Lab
      {% if hidden > 0 %} &middot; +{{ hidden | escape }} not shown{% endif %}
      {% if cloud != "connected" %} &middot; cloud {{ cloud | replace: "_", " " | escape }}{% endif %}
      {% if updated_at %} &middot; {{ updated_at | slice: 11, 5 | escape }} UTC{% endif %}
    </span>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The same information for a shared screen, where a permanent bar would cost
  more room than it earns. Rendered only when there is something the viewer
  could not otherwise work out, and then without the branding or the clock.
{% endcomment %}
{% template plugin_note %}
  {% if hidden > 0 or cloud != "connected" %}
    <span class="label">
      {% if hidden > 0 %}+{{ hidden | escape }} not shown{% endif %}
      {% if hidden > 0 and cloud != "connected" %} &middot; {% endif %}
      {% if cloud != "connected" %}cloud {{ cloud | replace: "_", " " | escape }}{% endif %}
    </span>
  {% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  A printer's supporting numbers, one per grid column. Each is guarded
  independently, so a printer reporting a bed but no nozzle shows one figure
  rather than a gap where the other would be.

  `.grid` rather than `.layout` or a bare `.item`. The framework gives
  `.layout` `container-type: size`, so a `.layout` that no parent is stretching
  reports zero height and its contents vanish; and the sibling gap inside a
  single `.item` is two pixels, which runs adjacent figures together into one
  unreadable string. `.grid` gives equal columns and the framework's own gap.
{% endcomment %}
{% template printer_stats %}
  <div class="grid">
    {% if printer.remaining %}
      <div class="item">
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ printer.remaining | escape }}</span>
          <span class="label">Remaining</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if printer.layer %}
      <div class="item">
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ printer.layer | escape }}{% if printer.layers %}/{{ printer.layers | escape }}{% endif %}</span>
          <span class="label">Layer</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if printer.nozzle %}
      <div class="item">
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ printer.nozzle | escape }}{% if printer.nozzle_target %}/{{ printer.nozzle_target | escape }}{% endif %}&deg;</span>
          <span class="label">Nozzle</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if printer.bed %}
      <div class="item">
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ printer.bed | escape }}{% if printer.bed_target %}/{{ printer.bed_target | escape }}{% endif %}&deg;</span>
          <span class="label">Bed</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if printer.material %}
      <div class="item">
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small">{{ printer.material | escape }}</span>
          <span class="label">Filament</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}
